  "body": "## What changed\n\n- recover filter flows immediately when the main browser page is hijacked to an external/ad domain\n- restore a last-known safe Vinted URL **before propagating filter errors**, so existing sort/price URL fallbacks can never append Vinted parameters to an external URL\n- make category/filter reload recover to the last trusted Vinted page instead of reloading an ad page\n- make Vinted host/catalog validation URI-based and HTTPS-only instead of permissive string matching\n- use the same strict host validation for popup/page classification\n- retry only bounded, transient Vinted navigation failures (`ERR_NETWORK_CHANGED`, `ERR_NAME_NOT_RESOLVED`, connection reset/timeout, interrupted navigation)\n- detect stopped worker-slot futures during scheduler sync and recreate missing concurrency capacity when RUNNING bots still require it\n- add lightweight tests for trusted/lookalike/external/non-HTTPS URL classification\n- add `playwright/REAL_ACTION_TESTING.md` with a staged DRY RUN -> PREFLIGHT ONLY -> one real action -> multi-bot test ladder\n\n## Why\n\nThe latest runtime log completed all 76 market-stat targets successfully, but one primary filter flow was repeatedly redirected from Vinted to `sos-accessoire.com` before the existing fallback recovered. The same log also proves two scheduler jobs can already run concurrently (`working=2`). Before enabling any real-action flags, this PR hardens the browser/filter boundary and makes worker-slot capacity self-healing.\n\n## Safety\n\n- no real-action flag is enabled by this PR\n- existing exact confirmation token and bot allowlist are unchanged\n- `PREFLIGHT_ONLY` behavior is unchanged\n- max 1 real first offer per catalog run remains unchanged\n- max 1 real next step per negotiation-check run remains unchanged\n- first-offer one-shot test mode remains unchanged\n- no production/continuous-real-action branch is merged\n\n## Validation\n\n- branch is based directly on current main\n- reviewed scheduler state machine: one bot remains QUEUED or WORKING, never both\n- current runtime log already demonstrated two different bots working simultaneously on two slots\n- URL safety unit tests cover Vinted, external URLs, lookalike hosts, non-HTTPS URLs and catalog-path validation\n- reviewed the external-redirect path through category, brand, model, sort and price actions; URL fallbacks see a restored trusted URL after page-safety failure\n- repository has no configured CI checks; local Maven execution is still unavailable in the assistant environment because its container cannot resolve GitHub/Maven dependencies",
